  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Vermont total $344M for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense leads buying activity with $204M. Contracting activity is concentrated in a few vendors and industries: GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC received $78.1M, Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing totaled $78.1M, and Engineering Services totaled $54.5M. Award volume to date is 4,326 with an average award size of $79.5K. Obligations are down 60.8% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Historical context shows peak obligations of $920M in FY24 and $877M in FY25 before the FY26 total of $344M. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $57M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $38.2M in FY2026 to date. Top vendors beyond GLOBALFOUNDRIES include SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION with $46.4M and MIND COMPUTING, INC. with $29.4M. These figures show where federal buying is concentrated by agency, vendor, and NAICS industry in Vermont for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Vermont federal contracting this year?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 60.8% year over year. The state recorded $344M in FY26 to date after $877M in FY25 and $920M in FY24. The Department of Defense continues to dominate buying, but total obligations this fiscal year are a smaller share of recent peaks."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who and what received the most federal money in Vermont this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $204M in FY2026 to date. GLOBALFOUNDRIES U.S. 2 LLC received $78.1M, Semiconductor and Related Device Manufacturing totaled $78.1M, and Engineering Services totaled $54.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
